# The EOL-tolerance hardening (R-ENG-23, registered at the N4 exit
# gate; landed as an N5 pre-check): text files check out LF on EVERY
# platform, killing the autocrlf class that cost the N4 windows lane
# its rounds 4-5 (the Windows runner's core.autocrlf converted the
# committed LF expected text to CRLF at checkout). `text=auto` keeps
# git's binary auto-detection; the explicit binary marks belt-and-
# brace the tree's binary classes (png/pdf/ico are the only classes
# present — verified by two isolated renormalize probes at the N5
# gate: zero content deltas). The smoke-side EOL normalization stays
# as belt-and-braces.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.exe binary
*.dylib binary
*.wasm binary
